  "abstract": "We isolate the part of the proto-spinor construction that is mathematically forced after its geometric premises are stated. A world-in-world field is a section of Hom (TP, TI) for oriented rank-three bundles; its nine local components do not multiply manifold dimensions. If closure data must retain the nontrivial loop class in SO(3), the faithful continuous double-cover carrier is spinorial and is represented through Spin (3) \u2245 SU(2). This is a conditional lifting theorem, not a derivation of internal dimension three or of physical fermions from admissibility alone. For the selected q79 degree-three spectral cover we record the exact trace split of ranks 1 + 2, the common 1 + 2 + 3 carrier, and the local binary-dihedral lift of signed sheet monodromy. The shared circle is now a specified pullback of one universal flat \u2124\u2086\u2084 differential line, not merely an isomorphic fiber. Its determinant, CLN, root-plane, and finite-Hessian actions intertwine exactly. The BHT and Hori fiber transforms share one orthogonal complex structure J_FM, and the binary sheet group has exactly two conjugate \u00b1i phase-root lifts for which the square of either signed i times J_FM is the identity. Strict global Spin closure remains equivalent to a branch-relator obstruction calculation; the closed result is SpinC and finite symbolic. Circle, lens, and nil remain typed phase, finite-transport, and anchoring roles. The later trace-plane construction supplies a Clifford module, and the selected framed product source admits two equivalent binary-root factorizations of its complete free Dirac carrier and observable net. We explain the exact finite 864 \u2192 96 reduction, conditional continuum and Deligne constructions, and selected finite family-response algebra without identifying dimensionless spectra with masses. A nonflat same-endpoint HYM comparison, interacting physical action, and strict source-selected magnitudes remain distinct downstream problems.",
